ADDRESS: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation
==================================================
[LINK: (Ford Foundation Building) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation_Building]  [LINK: (New York City) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City] ,  [LINK: (New York) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_(state)] , U.S.

The Ford Foundation is an American  [LINK: (private foundation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Private_foundation]  with the stated goal of advancing human welfare. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation#cite_note-3]  [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation#cite_note-Overview-4]  [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation#cite_note-5]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation#cite_note-wellesley-6]  Created in 1936 [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation#cite_note-dietrich-7]  by  [LINK: (Edsel Ford) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edsel_Ford]  and his father  [LINK: (Henry Ford) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Ford] , it was originally funded by a $25,000 (about $550,000 in 2023) gift from Edsel Ford. [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation#cite_note-Overview-4]  By 1947, after the death of the two founders, the foundation owned 90% of the  [LINK: (non-voting shares) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-voting_shares]  of the  [LINK: (Ford Motor Company) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Motor_Company] ; the Ford family retained the voting shares. [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation#cite_note-funding-8]  Between 1955 and 1974, the foundation sold its Ford Motor Company holdings and now plays no role in the automobile company.

In 1949,  [LINK: (Henry Ford II) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Ford_II]  created  [LINK: (Ford Philanthropy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Philanthropy] , a separate corporate foundation that to this day serves as the philanthropic arm of the Ford Motor Company and is not associated with the Ford Foundation.

For many years, the Ford Foundation's  [LINK: (financial endowment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_endowment]  was the largest private endowment in the world; it remains among the  [LINK: (wealthiest) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_wealthiest_charitable_foundations] . For fiscal year 2023, it reported assets of $16.8 billion and expenses of $852 million. [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation#cite_note-financials-2]


