# FURTHER READING #

Berman, Edward H. The Ideology of Philanthropy: The influence of the Carnegie, Ford, and Rockefeller foundations on American foreign policy, State University of New York Press, 1983.

[LINK: (Napoleon, Davi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Davi_Napoleon] .  [LINK: (Chelsea on the Edge: The Adventures of an American Theater) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chelsea_on_the_Edge:_The_Adventures_of_an_American_Theater] . The Ford Foundation gave the Chelsea Theater a grant in the early 1970s that enabled the theater to do groundbreaking multimedia work. The funding was abruptly halted after three years, an event that along with decreased funding from the  [LINK: (National Endowment for the Arts) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Endowment_for_the_Arts]  helped precipitate the theater's collapse. This is a history that explores the on-stage and backstage dramas at the Chelsea, with special attention to how theaters are funded.

Chester, Eric Thomas. Covert Network, Progressives, the International Rescue Committee and the CIA,  M. E. Sharpe, 1995, Routledge, 2015.

Dezalay, Yves, and Bryant G. Garth, The Internationalization of Palace Wars: lawyers, economists, and the contest to transform Latin American states, Chicago: University of Chicago Press, 2002.

Feldman, Bob. "Alternative Media Censorship sponsored by CIA's Ford Foundation?" at the  [LINK: (Wayback Machine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine]  (archived 2005-04-07)

Parmar, Inderjeet, Foundations of the American Century: The Ford, Carnegie, and Rockefeller Foundations in the Rise of American Power. New York: Columbia University Press, 2012.

Petras, James (2001). "The Ford Foundation and the CIA".

Ransom, David (1975). "Ford Country: Building an Elite for Indonesia". In Weissman, Steve; Members of the Pacific Studies Center; Members of the North American Congress on Latin America (eds.). The Trojan Horse: A Radical Look at Foreign Aid. Ramparts Press Reader Series (Revised ed.). Palo Alto, Calif.: Ramparts Press. pp. 93–116.  [LINK: (ISBN) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)]   [LINK: (0878670602) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/0878670602] .  [LINK: (LCCN) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LCCN_(identifier)]  72-75809.  [LINK: (OCLC) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OCLC_(identifier)]  1217505. Retrieved January 31, 2026. "Ford Country: Building an Elite for Indonesia" at  [LINK: (archive.today) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archive.today]  (archived 21 December 2012).

[Rockefeller Foundation; Ford Foundation;  [LINK: (Carnegie Foundation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnegie_Corporation_of_New_York] ;  [LINK: (Council on Foreign Relations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_on_Foreign_Relations] ]. "Time for Ford Foundation & CFR to Divest?" at the  [LINK: (Wayback Machine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine]  (archived 2006-08-13), collaboration of the Rockefeller, Ford and Carnegie Foundations with the  [LINK: (Council on Foreign Relations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_on_Foreign_Relations] .

